Hello,

Here's a small C library that mixes and plays sound samples in real-time.
It's currently limited to 4 channels.

This library could be a starting point for sound apps that respond in
somewhat real-time to user input.  Included is a really dumb drum machine
demo, but the library can also be used to easily add sound to games.

Required:
Linux, a soundcard with digital sample playback, and voxware 
2.9 or greater (voxware is the kernel sound drivers)
Do a 'cat /dev/sndstat' to see what version you have.

As soon as I can get on, I'll upload it to:

sunsite.unc.edu:/pub/Linux/Incoming/soundIt0.02.tar.gz

Currently available at imagineer.disc-net.com:

198.162.12.57:/pub/pitzel/soundIt0.02.tar.gz

thanks,
--brad
pitzel@cs.sfu.ca

