tested.

	The Fall release also has a new kernel facility written by
Ross Biro at Yggdrasil that allows the kernel to use BIOS and
DOS (MSCDEX) to access hard disks and CDROM drives that are not
directly supported by Linux.  The reliability of this facility is
dependent on how well behaved the BIOS or MSCDEX driver being used
