all /etc/passwd entries and queries the NIS server all the time,
even if you haven't put a + entry in your passwd file.
This is not the way it should be done.

My advice is to either disable NIS or insure (via /etc/yp.conf) that
only trusted servers are queried. Especially the ypset feature
should be disabled...

