I've placed a new and improved version of the OTI-087 driver for SVGALIB 
on sunsite.unc.edu (/pub/Linux/Incoming/svgalib_OTI-087_1.2.tar.gz).  
It'll eventually move to /pub/Linux/libs/graphics, I think.

THIS DRIVER IS NOT FOR X.  SVGALIB is a graphics library that allows 
non-X programs to use SVGA modes (examples are GhostScript and 
sasteroids).  My driver allows SVGALIB to properly utilize the features 
of the Oak OTI-087 SVGA chipset.

What's new:
640x480x32K and 800x600x32K modes.
