I have uploaded new versions of my Tcl/Tk shared libraries for Linux
to sunsite.unc.edu.  See the LSM entries below for the exact file
names and locations.  Here is the summary of changes from the previous
versions:

  Shared library support is now integrated into the normal Makefiles
  (i.e. no more make.* shell scripts).  In most cases, "make install"
  does everything.  TclX requires a couple of extra steps because of
  its need to use itself in the installation process.

  The installation directory can be chosen using the --prefix option
  when running configure.  My pre-compiled versions were configured
  for /usr/local.  Linux distributors should recompile using /usr or
